---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Open source | Gatebridge">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose-page">
      <h1>Open source</h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted">
        Gatebridge is open-core. The server program, the Android app, and the
        message protocol are open source. The hosted service and admin tools
        are the paid product.
      </p>

      <h2>The split</h2>
      <div class="split-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Open source (free forever)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Linux server program source</li>
            <li>Android app source</li>
            <li>Message protocol (PROTOCOL.md)</li>
            <li>Relay configuration examples</li>
            <li>Build and deployment scripts</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="https://github.com/andreparames/fido2-android-bridge" class="btn btn-secondary mt-4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            View on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Paid product (managed convenience)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Pre-built Play Store app with auto-updates</li>
            <li>Hosted encrypted relay</li>
            <li>Admin console and device registry</li>
            <li>Team management and audit log</li>
            <li>Support (email and Slack)</li>
          </ul>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary mt-4" data-waitlist>Get notified</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Why this model</h2>
      <p>
        You can run Gatebridge entirely for free: clone the repo, build the
        server program, sideload the app, and run your own relay. That route
        has real friction: run the relay software, manage certificates, handle
        app updates, manage pairing. The paid product removes that friction.
        This is the same trade as Ghost or Mattermost: open source is not the
        same as a free hosted service.
      </p>

      <h2>License</h2>
      <p>
        The open-source parts use a permissive license. See the repository for
        the current choice. The hosted service we run for customers is
        proprietary.
      </p>

      <h2>Contributing</h2>
      <p>
        Contributions are welcome. The codebase uses strict test-driven
        development. See the repository's CONTRIBUTING.md and the architecture
        plans for context.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .prose-page h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .prose-page ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
  }

  .prose-page li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .split-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }

  .split-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .split-grid ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .split-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
